// Generated by scripts/generate-api-docs.mjs from docs/openapi.yaml. Do not edit; run `yarn docs:generate`.
export const AGENT_DOCS_MARKDOWN = "# Hoardwise API\n\nThe Hoardwise budget API. Every route is under `/api` and speaks JSON.\n\n## Amounts, dates and months\n\n- Amounts are integers in the smallest currency unit (pence or cents), never decimals. A transaction, target,\n  pot or recurring amount is positive and at most 1,000,000,000. Account balances are sent as `pence`.\n- Dates are `YYYY-MM-DD`, months are `YYYY-MM` and timestamps are ISO 8601.\n\n## Glossary\n\n- Transaction `type`: `EXPENSE` is Spend, `INCOME` is Income, `SET_ASIDE` is Add to pot and `TAKE_OUT` is\n  Take from pot.\n- A budget is a category target (`/api/targets`), weekly or monthly.\n- A pot is a category whose balance carries over from month to month.\n\n## Examples and the clock\n\nPot and recurring examples assume the server clock is in October 2026 (UTC). `listPots`, `putPot` and\n`archivePot` reject a month more than one month away from the server's current UTC month, so the `2026-10`\nvalues in those examples fail outside September to November 2026.\n\nThe `addAccountBalance` example records a balance on 2026-10-29; the date may be at most one day after the\nserver's current UTC date, so it fails if the clock is before 28 October 2026.\n\n## Authentication\n\nThere are two ways to authenticate, and every operation accepts either unless its `x-token-access` says otherwise.\n\n- A browser session: the Auth0 JWT as a Bearer token (Auth0 mode), or the session cookie set by the built-in\n  login (local mode). Cookie-authenticated requests that change data must send an `Origin` header matching the\n  app's origin (`APP_ORIGIN` when set, otherwise the host).\n- A personal API token, created on the Access tokens page or with `POST /api/tokens`, sent as\n  `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. A read token starts `hwr_` and a read-write token starts `hww_`. Examples in this\n  document use placeholders such as `hwr_EXAMPLE`; never paste a real token into shared text.\n\nToken rules:\n\n- A read token may only make `GET` and `HEAD` requests. Any other method returns 403\n  `This token is read-only`. A read-write token may use every method.\n- A token can never reach `/api/tokens*`, `/api/push*` or `/api/auth/*`; those return 403\n  `Not available to access tokens`. Each operation records this as `x-token-access`: `none` (no token),\n  `read` (a read token is enough) or `write` (a read-write token is needed).\n- A token is shown once when it is created, expires when its owner chose, can be revoked, and in local mode\n  is revoked for good by a password reset (AUTH-15; Auth0 mode has no local password reset).\n- Repeated failed token lookups from one client address are rate limited and answered with 429 and a\n  `Retry-After` header. The limit is exact in the self-hosted container and best-effort per instance on AWS.\n\n`/api/auth/*` (login, logout, setup and recovery for the built-in login) is not described here.\n\n## Errors\n\nAn error response has a JSON body `{ \"error\": \"<message>\" }`, and some add extra fields. The statuses are 400\n(invalid input), 401 (missing or invalid credential), 403 (forbidden, including token limits and protected\ndefault categories), 404 (unknown route or record), 409 (conflict with the current state), 429 (too many\nrequests; see `Retry-After`) and 500 (an unexpected server failure, with a generic message).\n\n## HEAD\n\n`HEAD` on any `GET` operation returns the same status and headers as `GET` with no body. `HEAD` operations are not\nlisted separately. A path with no `GET` operation (for example `/api/categories/{categoryId}/reassign`) and an\nunknown path answer `HEAD` with 404, as they do `GET`.\n\n## categories\n\nSpending and income categories, including pot categories.\n\n### GET /api/categories\n\nList categories\n\nToken access: read\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The default and custom categories.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### POST /api/categories\n\nCreate a custom category\n\nToken access: write\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `name` (string, required): Trimmed, then 1 to 50 characters.\n- `type` (string (EXPENSE|INCOME|POT), required)\n- `icon` (string, optional): An emoji or icon name, cut to 50 characters.\n- `group` (string (BILLS|SINKING_FUNDS|EVERYDAY|SAVING_INVESTMENT), optional): Not allowed for `INCOME`.\n\nResponses:\n- 201: The category was created.\n- 400: The request was invalid.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### PUT /api/categories/{categoryId}\n\nRename a custom category\n\nToken access: write\n\nParameters:\n- `categoryId` (path, required): string. The id of a category.\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `name` (string, required): Trimmed, then 1 to 50 characters.\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The renamed category.\n- 400: The request was invalid.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: A default category cannot be renamed (`Cannot rename a default category`), or the credential may not make this request (see the shared `Forbidden` response).\n- 404: No custom category has this id (`Category not found`).\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### DELETE /api/categories/{categoryId}\n\nDelete a custom category\n\nToken access: write\n\nParameters:\n- `categoryId` (path, required): string. The id of a category.\n\nResponses:\n- 204: The category is gone.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: A default category cannot be deleted (`Cannot delete a default category`), or the credential may not make this request (see the shared `Forbidden` response).\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### POST /api/categories/{categoryId}/reassign\n\nMove a category's transactions and reminders to another category\n\nToken access: write\n\nParameters:\n- `categoryId` (path, required): string. The id of a category.\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `toCategoryId` (string, required): The category to move records to.\n\nResponses:\n- 200: How many records were moved.\n- 400: The request was invalid.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n## transactions\n\nSpend, income and pot movements.\n\n### GET /api/transactions\n\nList a month's transactions\n\nToken access: read\n\nParameters:\n- `year` (query, required): integer. The four-digit year, 2000 or later.\n- `month` (query, required): integer. The month number, 1 to 12.\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The month's transactions (an empty list when there are none).\n- 400: `year` or `month` is missing (`year and month query parameters are required`) or not a four-digit year of 2000 or later and a month from 1 to 12 (`Invalid year or month`).\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### POST /api/transactions\n\nAdd a transaction\n\nToken access: write\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `transactionId` (string, optional): Create only, a client-chosen UUID.\n- `amount` (integer, required): Positive integer pence (or cents).\n- `type` (string (EXPENSE|INCOME|SET_ASIDE|TAKE_OUT), required): What kind of movement this is.\n- `categoryId` (string, required): Not checked against existing categories.\n- `description` (string|null, optional): Optional, at most 200 characters before trimming.\n- `date` (string, required): `YYYY-MM-DD`, a real calendar date (`2026-02-30` is rejected).\n- `recurringId` (string|null, optional): Links the transaction to a recurring reminder (a UUID); not checked against existing reminders.\n\nResponses:\n- 201: The transaction was stored.\n- 400: The request was invalid.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### GET /api/transactions/range\n\nList transactions across several months\n\nToken access: read\n\nParameters:\n- `from` (query, required): string. The first month, as `YYYY-MM`.\n- `to` (query, required): string. The last month, as `YYYY-MM`.\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The transactions in the range (an empty list when there are none).\n- 400: `from` or `to` is missing or not a month (`from and to must be months in YYYY-MM format`), `from` is after `to` (`from must not be after to`), or the range is over 24 months (`the range must be at most 24 months`).\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### PUT /api/transactions/{yearMonth}/{transactionId}\n\nReplace a transaction\n\nToken access: write\n\nParameters:\n- `yearMonth` (path, required): string. The month a transaction belongs to, as `YYYY-MM`, with a month from 01 to 12.\n- `transactionId` (path, required): string. The id of a transaction.\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `transactionId` (string, optional): Create only, a client-chosen UUID.\n- `amount` (integer, required): Positive integer pence (or cents).\n- `type` (string (EXPENSE|INCOME|SET_ASIDE|TAKE_OUT), required): What kind of movement this is.\n- `categoryId` (string, required): Not checked against existing categories.\n- `description` (string|null, optional): Optional, at most 200 characters before trimming.\n- `date` (string, required): `YYYY-MM-DD`, a real calendar date (`2026-02-30` is rejected).\n- `recurringId` (string|null, optional): Links the transaction to a recurring reminder (a UUID); not checked against existing reminders.\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The updated transaction.\n- 400: The request was invalid.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 404: No transaction with this id exists in the path month (`Transaction not found`).\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### DELETE /api/transactions/{yearMonth}/{transactionId}\n\nDelete a transaction\n\nToken access: write\n\nParameters:\n- `yearMonth` (path, required): string. The month a transaction belongs to, as `YYYY-MM`, with a month from 01 to 12.\n- `transactionId` (path, required): string. The id of a transaction.\n\nResponses:\n- 204: The transaction is deleted.\n- 400: The path `yearMonth` is not in `YYYY-MM` format (`yearMonth must be in YYYY-MM format`).\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n## targets\n\nBudgets (category targets), weekly or monthly, one per category.\n\n### GET /api/targets\n\nList budgets\n\nToken access: read\n\nResponses:\n- 200: All targets.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### PUT /api/targets/{categoryId}\n\nSet a category's budget\n\nToken access: write\n\nParameters:\n- `categoryId` (path, required): string. The id of a category.\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `targetAmount` (integer, required): Positive integer pence (or cents).\n- `period` (string (MONTHLY|WEEKLY), required)\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The stored target.\n- 400: The request was invalid.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 404: No category has this id (`Category not found`).\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### DELETE /api/targets/{categoryId}\n\nRemove a category's budget\n\nToken access: write\n\nParameters:\n- `categoryId` (path, required): string. The id of a category.\n\nResponses:\n- 204: The target is removed.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n## pots\n\nPot settings, balances and archiving.\n\n### GET /api/pots\n\nList pots with balances\n\nToken access: read\n\nParameters:\n- `asOf` (query, required): string. The month to work out balances for, as `YYYY-MM`.\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The pots (abridged in this example; the real list has one entry for every pot category).\n- 400: `asOf` is missing, not a `YYYY-MM` month, or more than one month ahead (`asOf must be a month in YYYY-MM format, at most one month ahead`).\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### PUT /api/pots/{categoryId}\n\nSet a pot's monthly amount, goal and automatic contribution\n\nToken access: write\n\nParameters:\n- `categoryId` (path, required): string. The id of a pot category, built-in (such as `cat-holidays`) or custom.\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `monthlyAmount` (integer|null, required): Positive integer pence, or null for none.\n- `goalAmount` (integer|null, required): Positive integer pence, or null for no goal.\n- `autoContribute` (boolean, required): Add `monthlyAmount` to the pot automatically every month from `month`.\n- `month` (string, required): The first month the automatic contribution change applies to, `YYYY-MM`.\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The stored settings (without storage keys).\n- 400: The body is not a JSON object (`Invalid JSON body`); `monthlyAmount` or `goalAmount` is missing or not null or a positive integer of at most 1,000,000,000 (`monthlyAmount must be null or a positive integer of pence`, and the same for `goalAmount`); `autoContribute` is not a boolean (`autoContribute must be a boolean`); `month` is missing, malformed or not within one month of now (`month must be a YYYY-MM month within one month of now`); `autoContribute` is true with a null `monthlyAmount` (`autoContribute needs a monthlyAmount`); `categoryId` is not a pot category (`categoryId must be an existing pot category`); or the history would exceed 120 entries (`Too many auto-contribute changes for this pot`).\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 409: The pot is archived (`Unarchive this pot before changing it`).\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### POST /api/pots/{categoryId}/archive\n\nArchive a pot\n\nToken access: write\n\nParameters:\n- `categoryId` (path, required): string. The id of a pot category, built-in (such as `cat-holidays`) or custom.\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `month` (string, required): The month the pot is emptied by, `YYYY-MM`.\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The pot is archived.\n- 400: The body is not a JSON object of exactly `{ month }`, or `month` is malformed or not within one month of now (`Body must be { month } as a YYYY-MM month within one month of now`); or `categoryId` is not a pot category (`categoryId must be an existing pot category`).\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 409: The pot still holds money (or is overdrawn).\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### POST /api/pots/{categoryId}/unarchive\n\nUnarchive a pot\n\nToken access: write\n\nParameters:\n- `categoryId` (path, required): string. The id of a pot category, built-in (such as `cat-holidays`) or custom.\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The pot's settings with `archivedAt` cleared.\n- 400: `categoryId` is not a pot category (`categoryId must be an existing pot category`).\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 409: The pot is not archived (`This pot is not archived`).\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n## recurring\n\nReminders for bills and income that repeat.\n\n### GET /api/recurring\n\nList recurring reminders\n\nToken access: read\n\nResponses:\n- 200: All recurring reminders.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### POST /api/recurring\n\nAdd a recurring reminder\n\nToken access: write\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `type` (string (EXPENSE|INCOME|SET_ASIDE|TAKE_OUT), required): What kind of movement this is.\n- `categoryId` (string, required): Not checked against existing categories.\n- `amount` (integer, required): Positive integer pence (or cents).\n- `description` (string|null, optional): Optional, at most 200 characters before trimming.\n- `frequency` (any, optional): Defaults to `MONTHLY` when omitted or null.\n- `dayOfMonth` (integer, optional): Required for `MONTHLY`.\n- `anchorDate` (string, optional): Required for the non-monthly frequencies, a real calendar date.\n- `leadDays` (integer|null, optional): Defaults to 3 when omitted or null.\n\nResponses:\n- 201: The reminder was created.\n- 400: The body is not a JSON object (`Invalid JSON body`) or a field breaks a rule.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### PUT /api/recurring/{recurringId}\n\nReplace a recurring reminder\n\nToken access: write\n\nParameters:\n- `recurringId` (path, required): string. The id of a recurring reminder.\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `type` (string (EXPENSE|INCOME|SET_ASIDE|TAKE_OUT), required): What kind of movement this is.\n- `categoryId` (string, required): Not checked against existing categories.\n- `amount` (integer, required): Positive integer pence (or cents).\n- `description` (string|null, optional): Optional, at most 200 characters before trimming.\n- `frequency` (any, optional): Defaults to `MONTHLY` when omitted or null.\n- `dayOfMonth` (integer, optional): Required for `MONTHLY`.\n- `anchorDate` (string, optional): Required for the non-monthly frequencies, a real calendar date.\n- `leadDays` (integer|null, optional): Defaults to 3 when omitted or null.\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The updated reminder.\n- 400: The reminder exists but the body is not a JSON object (`Invalid JSON body`) or breaks a rule listed under `createRecurring`.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 404: No reminder has this id (`Recurring item not found`).\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### DELETE /api/recurring/{recurringId}\n\nDelete a recurring reminder\n\nToken access: write\n\nParameters:\n- `recurringId` (path, required): string. The id of a recurring reminder.\n\nResponses:\n- 204: The reminder is deleted.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### POST /api/recurring/{recurringId}/handled\n\nMark a reminder handled, or clear the mark\n\nToken access: write\n\nParameters:\n- `recurringId` (path, required): string. The id of a recurring reminder.\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `period` (string|null, required): `YYYY-MM` (for monthly reminders), a real `YYYY-MM-DD` date (for the others) or null to clear.\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The updated reminder.\n- 400: The reminder exists but the body is not a JSON object (`Invalid JSON body`), `period` is missing or is neither a string nor null (`period must be YYYY-MM, YYYY-MM-DD or null`), or the string is the wrong format for the reminder's frequency (`period must be a YYYY-MM month for a monthly item`, or `period must be a real YYYY-MM-DD date for a weekly, four-weekly, quarterly or yearly item`).\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 404: No reminder has this id (`Recurring item not found`).\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n## accounts\n\nSavings, investments and debts, with a balance history.\n\n### GET /api/accounts\n\nList accounts\n\nToken access: read\n\nResponses:\n- 200: All accounts.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### POST /api/accounts\n\nAdd an account\n\nToken access: write\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `name` (string, required): 1 to 50 characters, not blank.\n- `kind` (string (ASSET|LIABILITY), required): `ASSET` is money held; `LIABILITY` is money owed.\n- `type` (string (CASH|SAVINGS|INVESTMENT|CREDIT_CARD|LOAN), required): `CASH`, `SAVINGS` and `INVESTMENT` belong to the `ASSET` kind; `CREDIT_CARD` and `LOAN` belong to the `LIABILITY` kind.\n\nResponses:\n- 201: The account was created.\n- 400: The body is not a JSON object (`Invalid JSON body`); `name` is missing, blank or over 50 characters (`name must be a non-empty string of at most 50 characters`); `kind` is not `ASSET` or `LIABILITY` (`kind must be ASSET or LIABILITY`); or `type` does not belong to `kind` (`type must match kind: CASH, SAVINGS, INVESTMENT` for an asset, `type must match kind: CREDIT_CARD, LOAN` for a liability).\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### PUT /api/accounts/{accountId}\n\nRename an account or change its type\n\nToken access: write\n\nParameters:\n- `accountId` (path, required): string. The id of an account.\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `name` (string, required): 1 to 50 characters, not blank.\n- `type` (string (CASH|SAVINGS|INVESTMENT|CREDIT_CARD|LOAN), required): `CASH`, `SAVINGS` and `INVESTMENT` belong to the `ASSET` kind; `CREDIT_CARD` and `LOAN` belong to the `LIABILITY` kind.\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The updated account.\n- 400: The body is not a JSON object (`Invalid JSON body`); `name` is missing, blank or over 50 characters (`name must be a non-empty string of at most 50 characters`); or `type` does not belong to the account's kind (`type must match the account's existing kind: CASH, SAVINGS, INVESTMENT` for an asset, `...\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 404: No account has this id (`Account not found`).\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### DELETE /api/accounts/{accountId}\n\nDelete an account\n\nToken access: write\n\nParameters:\n- `accountId` (path, required): string. The id of an account.\n\nResponses:\n- 204: The account is deleted.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### POST /api/accounts/{accountId}/balances\n\nRecord an account balance\n\nToken access: write\n\nParameters:\n- `accountId` (path, required): string. The id of an account.\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `date` (string, required): A real calendar date, `YYYY-MM-DD`, no later than tomorrow (UTC).\n- `pence` (integer, required): Integer pence (or cents); zero and negative values are allowed.\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The account with the balance recorded.\n- 400: The body is not a JSON object (`Invalid JSON body`); `date` is not a real `YYYY-MM-DD` date or is more than one day ahead (`date must be a YYYY-MM-DD date, at most one day ahead of today`); `pence` is not a whole number between -1,000,000,000 and 1,000,000,000 (`pence must be a whole number between -1000000000 and 1000000000`); or the account already has 500 entries on other dates (`an account can have at most 500 balance entries`).\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 404: No account has this id (`Account not found`).\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n## trash\n\nDeleted items that can be restored.\n\n### GET /api/trash\n\nList recently deleted items\n\nToken access: read\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The restorable items.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### POST /api/trash/restore\n\nRestore a deleted item\n\nToken access: write\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `entityType` (string (TRANSACTION|TARGET|RECURRING|ACCOUNT), required): What was deleted.\n- `id` (string, required): The `id` from `listTrash`.\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The item was restored.\n- 400: The body is not a JSON object (`Invalid JSON body`), has a field other than `entityType` and `id` (`Only entityType and id are allowed`), has a missing or unknown `entityType` (`entityType must be one of TRANSACTION, TARGET, RECURRING, ACCOUNT`), or has a missing or malformed `id` (`id is missing or not in the expected format`).\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: The credential is valid but may not do this: a read token on a write method, a token on a route tokens cannot use, a cross-origin cookie request, or a protected default category.\n- 404: Nothing with this type and id is in the trash, or it has expired or was just restored by another request (`This item is no longer in Recently deleted`).\n- 409: A record already exists at the original key, so nothing was restored and the item stays in the trash (`This item is already in place, so it was not restored`).\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n## push\n\nWeb push reminder subscriptions. Not available to access tokens.\n\n### POST /api/push/subscriptions\n\nTurn on bill reminders for a device\n\nToken access: none\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `subscription` (object, required): The browser's push subscription.\n  - `endpoint` (string, required): An https address, with no user name, password or port, on a supported push service: `fcm.googleapis.com`, `updates.push.services.mozilla.com`, `web.push.apple.com` or a host ending `.notify.windows.com`.\n  - `expirationTime` (any, optional): Accepted, as sent by browsers, but ignored.\n  - `keys` (object, required)\n    - `p256dh` (string, required): The browser's public key, base64url text.\n    - `auth` (string, required): The browser's auth secret, base64url text.\n- `settings` (object, required)\n  - `hour` (integer, required): The hour of the day (in `timeZone`) to send reminders.\n  - `quietStart` (integer|null, required): The hour quiet time starts, or null for no quiet hours.\n  - `quietEnd` (integer|null, required): The hour quiet time ends, or null for no quiet hours.\n  - `timeZone` (string, required): An IANA time zone name the platform recognises, such as `Europe/London`.\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The device is subscribed (created or updated).\n- 400: The body is not a JSON object (`Invalid JSON body`) or breaks a rule.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: An access token was used (`Not available to access tokens`), or a cookie-authenticated request came from another origin.\n- 409: Five other devices already have reminders on (`At most 5 devices can have reminders turned on`).\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### DELETE /api/push/subscriptions\n\nTurn off bill reminders for a device\n\nToken access: none\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `endpoint` (string, required): The endpoint to remove; it must pass the same allow-list as in `PushSubscriptionInput`.\n\nResponses:\n- 204: The device has no reminders.\n- 400: The body is not a JSON object, or holds a field other than `endpoint` (`Invalid JSON body`); or `endpoint` is not an https address of a supported push service (`endpoint must be an https address of a supported push service`).\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: An access token was used (`Not available to access tokens`), or a cookie-authenticated request came from another origin.\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n## tokens\n\nPersonal API token management. Not available to access tokens.\n\n### GET /api/tokens\n\nList access tokens\n\nToken access: none\n\nResponses:\n- 200: The tokens.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: An access token was used (`Not available to access tokens`), or the request was refused for another reason (see the shared `Forbidden` response).\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### POST /api/tokens\n\nCreate an access token\n\nToken access: none\n\nRequest body (JSON):\n- `name` (string, required): A label, at most 60 characters after trimming.\n- `scope` (string (read|write), required)\n- `expiryDays` (integer,null (90|180|365|730|), required): Days until the token expires, or null for never.\n- `password` (string, optional): The account password.\n\nResponses:\n- 201: The token was created.\n- 400: The body is not a JSON object (`Invalid JSON`) or breaks a rule.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: An access token was used (`Not available to access tokens`); in local mode a `write` token was requested without the account password (`Password required`) or with the wrong one (`Incorrect password`); or the request was refused for another reason (see the shared `Forbidden` response).\n- 409: The household already has 25 tokens (`You can have at most 25 access tokens.\n- 429: Too many requests (`Too many requests`, with `Retry-After`, as in the shared `TooManyRequests` response), or, in local mode when creating a `write` token, too many wrong passwords (`Too many attempts`).\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n\n### DELETE /api/tokens/{tokenId}\n\nRevoke an access token\n\nToken access: none\n\nParameters:\n- `tokenId` (path, required): string. The id of an access token.\n\nResponses:\n- 204: The token is revoked.\n- 401: The credential is missing, invalid, expired or revoked.\n- 403: An access token was used (`Not available to access tokens`), or the request was refused for another reason (see the shared `Forbidden` response).\n- 404: No token of this household has this id (`Token not found`).\n- 429: Too many requests.\n- 500: An unexpected failure.\n";
